WEBVTT

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
The Target Is Ikuto!?

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Gotsumon's Scheme

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.040
The Target Is Ikuto!?

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.550
Gotsumon's Scheme!

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.950
Our heroes battled with Mercurimon at Infinity Ice Ridge.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.110
Facing an enemy with such power put Masaru and the others in grave danger.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:37.870
It was the mysterious old man with the Digivice and his partner Gawappamon who saved them.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.720
Digisoul Charge!

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:46.720
Kamemon, evolve!

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.170
Gawappamon, yeah!

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.230
DJ Shooter!

00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:02.010
Covering for them, he urged Masaru, Ikuto, Falcomon, as well as the others, to return to the human world.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.070
Take care of Ikuto.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.940
Bring him back to the human world!

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.020
Old man!

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.110
Masaru, quickly!

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.320
Hurry up!

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.400
Masaru, c'mon!

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.400
Old man!

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.120
Let go of me!

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.120
Let go of me!

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.060
You not touch me!

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.420
I not let you!

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.590
Quit moving! Calm down!

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.630
I've gotta go!

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.840
You can't leave yet!

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.180
But I've gotta go!

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:40.960
You...!

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.530
Let go of me!

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.020
Let go of me!

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.060
Let go!

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.060
Let go!

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.720
Calm down!

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.300
I go back!

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.490
Go back to Digital World!

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.760
That's right!

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.910
I'm going to the Digital World right now to save that old man!

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:54.980
It's no use!

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.360
Even if you return to the Digital World now, there's nothing you can do.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.570
Are you giving up on the old man?!

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.420
The Chief would not wish for us to act rashly!

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.040
He Dove into the Digital World knowing fully well that this may happen!

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.580
"Chief?"

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.000
You mean that old man, do you, Captain?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.350
Tohma! Yoshino!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.120
That's right.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.970
That same man you met back in the Digital World...

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.760
is an expert in the field of Digimon crimes...

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.820
and the former Captain of the exploration squad in the Digital World.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.520
Holding the highest rank in DATS,

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.480
he is Chief Yushima.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.980
No way...

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.620
Why are you guys acting so calmly about this?

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.640
He appeared in the Digital World and made Kamemon evolve.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.960
That alone led me to conclude that he wasn't the average person.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.300
But to think that he was the Chief of DATS...

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.550
I had no idea...

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:52.200
So this means that the old man is our ally!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.750
That gives us all the more reason to go save him!

00:02:54.890 --> 00:03:00.220
If you go back without developing any strategies first, you will only be repeating the same mistakes.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.530
Until further instructions, the Dive to the Digital World will be closed!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.180
You two should hurry up and let these men finish your health inspection.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.010
Understood?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.180
Let go of me, you...!

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.150
Let go!!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.980
Aniki!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.070
What are you planning to do to us?

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.610
Nothing at all.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.210
The existence of Digimon is a secret in the human world.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:26.190
You can't go wandering around the city on your own.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.130
Why do you keep it a secret?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.830
To avoid chaos.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.750
Stop! Let go!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.250
Yoshino, Tohma. Let's listen to your reports.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.750
Yes, sir!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.750
Yes, sir!

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.760
We returned to the human world using the Digital Gate located at Infinity Ice Ridge.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.880
News on Mercurimon, Chief Yushima, and Kamemon is uncertain.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.720
That is all.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.540
Is that so?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.520
Thank you for your hard work.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.680
H-Hey, wait!

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.230
What on earth are you two doing?!

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.040
Work!

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.360
Man, this is so annoying!

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.640
Work, you bastard!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.240
Don't be so rash!

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.320
You, too! Get out of there!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.880
What are you doing? Don't go touching the transportation equipment whenever you feel like it!

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.450
Don't get in my way!

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.790
I'm going back to the Digital World right now!

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:13.870
I'm saving that old man!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.120
Stop it, Masaru!

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.840
You always mess up the machines whenever you touch them!

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.160
Damn it...

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:20.920
Work!

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.760
Work!

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:29.930
They broke it...

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.220
They really did...

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.230
Damn it, move!

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.060
Damn... Look at what you've done!

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.020
Now <i>I'm</i>  the one who has to repair everything!

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.470
Okay, my bad!

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.710
I'm sorry, so... hurry up and fix it!

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:42.980
Two weeks.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.280
Fixing it completely will take two whole weeks!

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.820
Wh-WHAT?!

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.040
C'mon, don't say that. Can't you do something?

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.570
Of course not.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.840
Not with this amount of destruction.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:58.830
No way!

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.790
Actually, things may be better off this way.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.720
Now that it's broken, you won't be able to sneak back.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.680
There's something I want to talk to you about.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.050
Talk? About what?

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.730
It's about the Digital World Exploration Squad.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.390
What I want to tell you is related to that boy, too.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.730
Related to Ikuto?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.890
The Digital World Exploration Squad,

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:26.970
consisting of the first humans to set foot into the Digital World, was known as the Project Team.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:32.370
The reason behind its formation was due to a string of events that occurred ten years ago.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:41.930
People began to disappear without warning one after the other, for no obvious reasons.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:47.750
No motives could be found behind their disappearances and there was no common link between them.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:52.440
The incidents were a perfect example of indiscriminate missing-persons cases.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:58.530
Recognizing the peril of these incidents, the Ministry of Confidentiality organized a special team.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.350
That was...

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:02.020
The Digital World Exploration Squad...

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.880
You could say they were the predecessors of DATS.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.820
Its members included Chief Yushima and me, who were both originally detectives of the police force.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:10.490
Detectives?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.820
Captain, you used to be a detective?

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.550
As for the civilians who accompanied us...

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:18.130
they were Masaru's father, Professor Daimon,

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:19.620
his assistant, Kurata-kun,

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.420
as well as the Noguchi couple, the leading experts in superspace research.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:29.630
The results from our team's collective inquiries and analysis thereof...

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:33.350
led us to discover the existence of another world.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.810
Which was... the Digital World.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.670
That's right.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:46.440
After concluding that this other world was the main factor behind the disappearances, we decided to continue our investigation in the Digital World.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.080
That was the beginning of hell.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:01.420
In the Digital World, our team faced difficulties one after the other.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.070
The Digimon constantly attacked...

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.390
Even our provisions were persistently in short supply...

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:21.730
Professor Daimon's whereabouts became unknown, as I'd mentioned previously.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:29.110
As for the Noguchi couple in the exploration squad...

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.860
They are...

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.920
that boy's parents.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:42.200
Ikuto's parents?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.060
What the... What do you mean?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.110
I had that boy's DNA examined.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.570
The results proved that he is the Noguchi couple's son.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.370
This subject is getting out of hand!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:57.440
I request a further explanation.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:02.340
The Noguchi couple were experts in superspace research, yet at the same time...

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.770
they were also victims of a missing-persons case.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.780
Their reason for participating in the exploration squad...

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:13.760
was because their newborn son had disappeared into the Digital World.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.700
Ikuto!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.430
Ikuto!!

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:26.890
Go and meet the Noguchi couple. They are currently residing in the Japanese Alps.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.110
Let go! Not going!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.770
My mother is no human!

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:32.680
Stop being so damn stubborn!

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.680
No matter how you look at it, you're human!

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.570
Wrong! I'm Digimon!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.530
Oh, now I've had it!

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.590
If you're gonna keep acting like this,

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:43.110
then I'll force you to understand that you're a human!

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:43.740
Come on!

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.150
Stop it!

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.170
That's right. Can't you see he doesn't like it?

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.160
Then what do you suggest we do?

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.480
There's no place where he belongs to in this world!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.050
<i>All of you will be smashed to pieces!</i>

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:05.060
In any case, you can't go back to the Digital World right away.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.120
You'll have to hang out with me for a little while.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.770
Or is there another place you want to go to?

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:13.590
If not, then don't complain, okay?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.690
Let's go.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:19.700
Those hateful humans...

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.070
What will you be doing now, my lord?

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.850
I am worried about Ikuto and Falcomon.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.200
I'd like to take them back first.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.380
In that case... in that case, let me handle the job!

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.120
Wh-What is this place?!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.230
Nice reaction.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.380
Not even country bumpkins are this enthusiastic.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.520
I'm no bumpkin! I'm Digimon!

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.900
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.460
From a Digital World that has nothing in it!

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.540
That's not true! Digital World has everything!

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.040
Oh, really? Then does it have that?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:04.850
Yeah!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.240
It's a painting full of data!

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.050
Wrong, that's a TV! There were things moving on the screen.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.210
I know! Falcomon is good at it.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.020
Being good or not has nothing to do with a TV!

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.350
Hmph! Mercurimon has hundred of those things!

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.230
Really?

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:20.420
Who the hell needs a hundred TVs?!

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:21.880
Well, he does!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:21.880
Yoshino...

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:22.670
Huh?!

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:26.170
How can anyone stand watching so much TV, anyway? It'll make your eyes go bad.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.900
Really, it's like there are two of Masaru in here.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.600
Just leave them alone for a few seconds and they start causing a ruckus.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.600
Staying cooped inside would make me go insane!

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.310
But...

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.750
I bet you not even have one!

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:32.950
Somehow the atmosphere is loosening up a bit.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.360
Of course we've got a TV around, at least! Nothing special, though.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:35.520
Those two are really something else.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.660
Must be small like everything else.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:38.030
What the... Say that once more, you bastard!

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.470
What a strange world this is...

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:48.600
There are so many humans around, and this vehicle is going so fast, but it's not hitting them...

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.410
Also...

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:04.950
Here's an announcement on the special event in stores where Hanamura Neon's new song will be sold!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.770
True to Hanamura Neon's talent, this new song...

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.670
Do you still feel sick?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.020
I'm okay...

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:19.570
Now...

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.230
Ah, Aniki.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.380
Here.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.640
You must be hungry.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.160
It's not poisoned or anything.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.370
Ikuto, this is delicious!

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.290
If you don't want it, I'll eat it all myself!

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.180
Finally, it's quiet...

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.480
This is why looking after kids is so tiring...

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:55.450
Geez...

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.070
Oh... so you were taking care of him.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.650
What's that tone supposed to mean?

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.440
Nothing really...

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.980
I just thought you seemed to be trying harder than usual.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:05.280
It's not that.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.660
Then what is it?

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.630
Since he has parents, I want him to meet them.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.130
That's all.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:13.620
That's true.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:23.430
Now that the Digital Gate at Infinity Ice Ridge is closed,

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:26.240
it's not that easy to go to the human world.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:30.470
By searching for a Gate, I'm losing my precious playtime.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.800
There must... there must be a way...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.060
This forest must be...

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.110
This is the worst.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:56.520
He was talking so maturely only seconds ago!

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.040
But in the end, he's just a kid himself!

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.140
And completely lacking in etiquette!

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:04.900
It's considered courtesy to pay attention to the driver's needs first!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.320
Making me do all the driving...

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.260
just because he's a student is no excuse!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.900
What does it matter? The fatigue must have caught up to him.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.420
I'm also <i>very</i>  fatigued myself.

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:18.230
I'd like to switch with you, but it'll be pretty useless...

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:21.560
Masaru is definitely <i>not</i>  popular with the girls.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.270
This is...

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:25.630
An emergency indicator.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.210
There's a Digimon signal to the north of your location.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:31.650
Alarm level 3, Area ND05.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:34.680
Currently, there is one Digimon signal.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.700
Wait!

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:36.910
What's wrong?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.250
There are more signals!

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.230
What the hell, Yoshino...

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:53.550
Can't you drive a bit better?

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:56.720
Be quiet! There's no time for that!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.250
A Digimon appeared!

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.100
What? Where?

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:03.400
It's really close. We should get there before any damage is done.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:04.760
Okay.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.110
Heh, I'm getting pumped!

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:34.180
Ookuwamon

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:34.180
Perfect Level

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.010
Ookuwamon.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.250
A Perfect Level Insect Digimon.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.630
It cuts everything with its mighty scissors.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:34.180
Its special attack is Scissor Arms Omega.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:44.780
Ikuto!

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.440
Find Ikuto!

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.540
Baby Flame!

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.300
At last! At last, you've appeared!

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.090
Gotsumon!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:09.070
Once I'm done with you in this battle,

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.050
you'll never be able to go back to the Digital World!

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.480
Go!

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:14.770
Let's go!

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:15.810
Yeah!

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:16.560
Lalamon!

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.050
Yes!

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:18.780
Digisoul...

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.300
Full Charge!

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.770
Lalamon, evolve!

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:50.920
Lilamon!

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:53.530
Masaru!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:54.170
Yeah!

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.080
Ikuto, let's go!

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.520
Gotsumon has come for us!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.400
Agumon!

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:15.530
Yeah!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.060
Digisoul Charge!

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:27.530
Agumon, evolve!

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:33.930
GeoGreymon!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.660
Ikuto, why aren't you coming?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.310
Because...

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.270
That's great!

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.810
Keep holding 'im down like that!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.920
Another level-up!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:00.760
Digisoul...

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.520
Full Charge!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.810
GeoGreymon, evolve!

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.180
RiseGreymon!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.340
Get 'im, RiseGreymon!

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.320
As long as I get Ikuto!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.030
Stop it!

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:47.670
What are you doing, Gotsumon?!

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.370
Aren't we allies?!

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:50.910
Don't be silly.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.030
Ikuto...

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.420
Ikuto must be eliminated!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.840
Why?

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.480
Ikuto has betrayed us!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.550
His cooperation with the humans is the ultimate proof!

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:03.260
No! It's not like that!

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.380
Yes, it is!

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:08.840
Our troubles with the human world have arisen because Ikuto exists!

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:11.600
The Digital World is wasted on the likes of Ikuto!

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.060
It's better if he was dead!

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:20.780
I...

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.660
Die!

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.500
Ikuto!

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.300
Oww...

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.350
You...

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:42.380
Man, stop making me look after you all the time!

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:49.990
Lilamon!

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:52.330
Marvel Shot!

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:04.650
Eat this!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:08.710
Unbelievable!

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:11.490
Unbelievable, they're beating the Ookuwamon one after another!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:21.950
Ookuwamon!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.090
Here... Here we retreat!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:25.310
Wait!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:27.000
We're not enemies!

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:30.380
Take us back with you to the Digital World!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.980
Absurd!

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:36.370
Ikuto's abominable existence only brings catastrophe to the Digital World!

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:40.020
He does not belong anywhere in the Digital World anymore!

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.940
This is the consensus of all of the Digimon!

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.790
Ikuto is a human.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:45.640
Yes,

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.070
a human!

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:58.540
Ikuto...

